<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<scheme version="2.0" title="DABAM2D example lens ID01" description="#********************************Undulator parameters (u27)&#10;    E=9000 # eV&#10;    numPer = 74 # Number of ID Periods&#10;    undPer = 0.027 # Period Length [m]&#10;&#10;    # e- beam paramters (RMS) EBS&#10;    sigEperE = 9.3E-4  # relative RMS energy spread&#10;    sigX = 30.3E-06  # horizontal RMS size of e-beam [m]&#10;    sigXp = 4.4E-06  # horizontal RMS angular divergence [rad]&#10;    sigY = 3.6E-06  # vertical RMS size of e-beam [m]&#10;    sigYp = 1.46E-06  # vertical RMS angular divergence [rad]&#10;    eBeam.partStatMom1.gamma = 6.00 / 0.51099890221e-03  # Relative Energy&#10;&#10;    z=117m    #first lens position&#10;&#10;    R = 50 * 1E-6          # Be CRL radius at the parabola appex&#10;    nCRL = args.n&#10;    CRLAph = 440 * 1E-6    # Be CRL aperture (thickness = 1mm)&#10;    CRLApv = 440 * 1E-6&#10;&#10;The profiles I would suggest are:&#10;&#10;https://github.com/oasys-esrf-kit/dabam2d/blob/main/data/dabam2d-0022.h5&#10;https://github.com/oasys-esrf-kit/dabam2d/blob/main/data/dabam2d-0023.h5&#10;https://github.com/oasys-esrf-kit/dabam2d/blob/main/data/dabam2d-0024.h5&#10;https://github.com/oasys-esrf-kit/dabam2d/blob/main/data/dabam2d-0025.h5&#10;&#10;You can use 4x lenses spaced 2mm from each other and check the image plane. If this is not sensitive enough (errors are not that high), I would suggest using the same EBS and undulator (maybe Z=100m) and 10x or 20x lenses and check the focal plane. In this case use the first N profiles;" working_directory="C:\Users\rafae\Oasys" workspace_units="0">
